// Any client with cis.read registers a callback for some datasets,
// optionally within a box. callback_url must be https (plain http
// only to localhost, and only with CISP_ALLOW_INSECURE_CALLBACKS),
// an absolute URL without userinfo or fragment, its host at most
// 253 characters, and neither a literal IP address nor a
// localhost, .local, .internal or .localhost name, nor a name that
// resolves to a loopback, private, link-local, CGNAT, multicast or
// unspecified address, unless CISP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_CALLBACKS (the
// lab). deliver applies the address rule again at every dial, to
// the address it connects to, and never follows a redirect. A
// client holds at most CISP_MAX_SUBSCRIPTIONS_PER_CLIENT (20)
// subscriptions that are not deleted; one more is 409 limit.
//
// The subscription is created pending_verification and deliver
// POSTs it a cis/change/v1 with reason subscription_test at once;
// the first 2xx makes it active. Until then GET says
// pending_verification and, in verification, the last attempt's
// status and error. Pending subscriptions are sent changes too.
//
