// (receivers in the ecosystem expose POST /v1/cis/notifications,
// but the CISP never assumes a path) as application/jose: a compact
// JWS (RS256, a kid of /.well-known/jwks.json) whose payload is
// {iss, aud, sub, iat, jti, body}: iss is CISP_ISSUER_URL, aud the
// host of callback_url without its port, sub the subscription id,
// jti the delivery id, and body the cis/change/v1 record (the
// Change schema). Receivers answer 2xx within 2 s; anything else,
// a redirect or a timeout is retried 1, 2, 4 ... s doubling to
// 300 s (with 10 % jitter) until 24 h after the change, then the
// delivery expires. 50 consecutive failures over at least an hour
// suspend an active subscription (its suspended_reason says since
// when and why). Receivers acknowledge reason subscription_test
// and republished, and any reason they do not know, with 204
// without pulling; only the publication and restriction reasons
// trigger a pull of pull_url, and only when its host is this
// CISP's. A notification is a hint: the subscriber still runs its
// own 60 s HEAD reconciliation.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/subscriptions (the `CreateSubscription` operationId).
